   267	## §4 RQ2 — Cross-Family Transfer (Leave-One-Family-Out CV)
   268	
   269	> **NEW 2026-09-27**: this section fills the RQ2 gap that PROGRESS_BRANCH §1
   270	> explicitly flagged as 0%. The pilot is **partial** — exploratory, one-step,
   271	> synthetic-only.
   272	
   273	**Setup.** 5-fold leave-one-family-out CV with multi-output
   274	`RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=200, max_depth=8, min_samples_leaf=5)`
   275	System-1 (one regressor per action; argmax = chosen action). Trained on
   276	`runs/phase8_6d_h3_20seed_5family.jsonl` (661 non-terminal records, 5 families
   277	× 20 seeds × horizon=3). Features: 15-dim state vector (12 numeric + 3 phase
   278	one-hot), via `scripts/_shared_rq_features.py` (shared with `exp_rq1_3_rf_probe.py`).
   279	
   280	**Baselines (all run on every held-out fold).**
   281	- **AlwaysSurrogate** (constant) — always picks `surrogate_acquisition`
   282	- **In-family RF** (LOSO reference, **not** an upper bound — see below)
   283	- **AlwaysLocal** (constant) — always picks `local_exploitation` (informational)
   284	- **RulePolicy (real, state-conditional)** — the actual `RulePolicy.select_action()` from
   285	  `src/opt_agent/loop/policies.py`: STOP if remaining_budget ≤ 4, GLOBAL_EXPLORATION
   286	  if stagnation_steps ≥ 3 AND budget ≥ 2, else SURROGATE_ACQUISITION. Reads state
   287	  from each record to produce a per-record action choice.
   288	
   289	**Metric.** Held-out decision regret = U(s, a*) − U(s, a_hat), where a_hat is
   290	the model's argmax over predicted utilities and a* is the oracle argmax.
   291	Lower is better.
   292	
   293	**Inference.** Per-family paired bootstrap 95% CIs in two flavors — (a)
   294	record-level (underestimates variance due to within-seed correlation) and (b)
   295	seed-block (resamples whole seeds with their records, preserving within-seed
   296	correlation; preferred per codex gpt-6-sol 2026-09-27 REVISE).
   297	
