   164	## §3 The v3 Framework
   165	
   166	Architecture diagram: `state → policy → action → backend → new_state`.
   167	
   168	### §3.1 Backend — `BocodeBotorchBackend`
   169	
   170	- BOCoDe problem + BoTorch SingleTaskGP + LogExpectedImprovement.
   171	- Single-objective, unconstrained, continuous box-bounded (audited allowlist).
   172	- Checkpoint / restore preserves GP state + RNG (`backend.checkpoint()`).
   173	- Optional **affine objective transform** `y → scale * y + shift` (Gate 5).
   174	
   175	### §3.2 State — `OptimizationState` (5 frozen dataclasses)
   176	
   177	```
   178	SamplingState        — n_samples, dimension, min_pairwise_distance, boundary_coverage
   179	SurrogateState       — is_current, validation_rmse (in-sample), mean/max posterior std (64-pt Sobol grid; NaN when unfitted)
   180	OptimizationProgress — best_value, last_value, recent_improvement, stagnation_steps
   181	ResourceState        — used/total/remaining budget, remaining_budget_ratio
   182	HistoryState         — last_action only (no action-sequence memory)
   183	```
   184	
   185	Frozen + JSON-safe (NaN→None); `to_payload()` exposes 15 keys for LLM
   186	prompts; the RF System-1 uses the same 15 numbers + 3 phase one-hots.
   187	Phase (early/mid/late) is derived downstream from remaining_budget_ratio,
   188	not stored. 2026-09-28: field list corrected to match
   189	`src/opt_agent/state/models.py` (the previous draft listed
   190	gap_to_best / last_n_actions / action_diversity, which were never
   191	implemented).
   192	
   193	### §3.3 Action — 8 typed `OptimizationAction`
   194	
   195	`global_exploration`, `local_exploitation`, `uncertainty_sampling`,
   196	`error_guided_sampling`, `boundary_sampling`, `surrogate_acquisition`,
   197	`retrain_surrogate`, `stop`. Each has fixed params, fixed eval cost,
   198	and an `execute_action` runner.
   199	
   200	### §3.4 Utility — 4-term weighted sum
   201	
   202	```
   203	U(a|s) = w_optimization · Δopt / σ_init
   204	       − w_evaluation · n_new_samples / total_budget
   205	       − w_fit · n_model_fits / total_budget
   206	       + w_stop_opportunity · I[STOP]
   207	P*(a|s) = softmax(U(a|s) / T)
   208	```
   209	
   210	Picked empirically per Phase 8.6A so that 1 sample ≈ 1/total_budget
   211	utility units, comparable to Δopt fractions.
   212	
   213	### §3.5 Counterfactual Rollout
   214	
   215	`CounterfactualRollout(s, candidates, horizon)` — for each candidate, runs
   216	`backend.restore(checkpoint) → execute(candidate) → run continuation policy
   217	for `horizon-1` steps → return utility`. Tries to restore on every step
   218	to keep the backend state clean.
   219	
   220	### §3.6 Decision Dataset — JSONL
   221	
   222	Each record: `state + candidate_actions + gold_probs + rollout_results +
   223	metadata + replay_checkpoint`. 423 unit tests cover the schema, generation,
   224	validation.
   225	
